# Machine-local i3 files — created/edited per box, not stowed.
# Listed here so `stow i3` (and install.sh) can't abort on them: one conflict
# aborts the WHOLE stow run, and install.sh runs with `set -eu`, so the script
# would die here (seen on the desktop 2026-09-29).
#
# NOTE: the repo still tracks i3/.config/i3/{local.conf,display.sh} from the era
# when machine-specific files lived in the package. They are leftovers — the
# templates live in examples/ — and they are what caused the conflict above.
# Removing them from git (git rm) is the proper cleanup; this ignore file is the
# safety net until that happens.
\.config/i3/local\.conf$
\.config/i3/display\.sh$
\.config/i3/machine\.env$
\.stow-local-ignore$
